    "id": "q_climate_20260228_010_4b93f0e0",
    "title": "When will the state of emergency be lifted in Boston following the 'Blizzard of 2026'?",
    "question_type": "timeframe",
    "options": [
      "2026-02-28T17:00:00Z"
    ],
    "background": "A massive blizzard, dubbed the 'Blizzard of 2026', has hit the northeastern United States, causing widespread disruption. A state of emergency has been declared in Boston to manage the situation. This question asks when the state of emergency will be lifted.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The question will resolve to the date when the Mayor of Boston officially lifts the state of emergency declared in response to the 'Blizzard of 2026'. The resolution will be based on official announcements from the Mayor's office or major news outlets.",
    "outcome": "2026-02-28T17:00:00Z",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe state of emergency in Boston following the historic 'Blizzard of 2026' was lifted on February 28, 2026, at 5:00 PM (17:00:00Z). The severity of the blizzard, dropping up to 3 feet of snow, necessitated massive snow removal and infrastructure repair efforts, which extended over several days. Once roads were sufficiently cleared and widespread power outages resolved, authorities determined that emergency measures were no longer needed. The formal lifting marked the transition from emergency response to standard recovery operations.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **2026-02-22 to 2026-02-24**: The Blizzard of 2026 strikes New England, dumping significant snow [art_general_20260224_006_1c057621].\n- **2026-02-24**: Massive cleanup efforts and power restorations begin [art_general_20260224_007_35a39377].\n- **2026-02-25 to 2026-02-27**: Intensive clearing of roads and critical infrastructure continues; discussions on ending emergency protocols [art_general_20260227_009_de05351e].\n- **2026-02-28T17:00:00Z**: The state of emergency is officially lifted for Boston [art_general_20260228_017_1ef9fe67].\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause was the unprecedented severity of the 'Blizzard of 2026', which caused extreme snow accumulation [art_general_20260224_010_a1147a0f]. This led to a mandatory state of emergency to facilitate rapid deployment of resources and enforce travel bans. Intermediate mechanisms involved multi-day cleanup operations to restore power and clear roads [art_general_20260224_007_35a39377]. The proximate trigger for lifting the order was the successful stabilization of city infrastructure, resulting in the final outcome where the emergency declaration was officially terminated on February 28 at 17:00:00Z [art_general_20260228_018_acb1ef73].\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nPersistent sub-freezing temperatures and secondary snow squalls threatened to prolong the emergency. However, these factors were overcome by round-the-clock plowing and the deployment of additional emergency crews from neighboring states.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- **E1**: The Blizzard of 2026 impacts Boston\n  - Date: 2026-02-24\n  - Why it matters: The root cause that required the emergency declaration.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_general_20260224_006_1c057621]\n- **E2**: Boston road and power infrastructure stabilized\n  - Date: 2026-02-27 to 2026-02-28\n  - Why it matters: Provided the necessary conditions for lifting the emergency.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_general_20260227_014_478b8345]\n- **E3**: State of emergency officially lifted\n  - Date: 2026-02-28\n  - Why it matters: The direct manifestation of the final outcome.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_general_20260228_017_1ef9fe67]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Blizzard causes extreme snow | [art_general_20260224_006_1c057621] | 2026-02-24 | 1.0 | Up to 3 feet of snow. |\n| Cleanup efforts progress | [art_general_20260224_007_35a39377] | 2026-02-24 | 1.0 | Schools and roads prioritized. |\n| Emergency lifted | [art_general_20260228_017_1ef9fe67] | 2026-02-28 | 1.0 | Marks the end of the emergency phase. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe exact hour the declaration was lifted could have varied based on localized unplowed secondary roads, but coordinated efforts allowed for the unified lifting on the target date.\n",
    "is_polymarket": false,
    "is_overlap": false,
    "market_open": "2026-02-24T00:00:00+00:00",
    "market_open_estimated": false,
    "market_close": "2026-02-28T23:59:59+00:00",
