    "id": "q_culture_20260128_003_fb3fd0e0",
    "title": "Will Courtney Love's documentary 'Antiheroine' premiere at the Sundance Film Festival in 2026?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "A documentary about Courtney Love, titled 'Antiheroine', is in production. Sundance is a likely premiere venue for such a film.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The premiere must be an official selection of the Sundance Film Festival. This is confirmed through the festival's official program.",
    "outcome": "True",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nCourtney Love's documentary *Antiheroine* premiered at the 2026 Sundance Film Festival. The documentary, directed by Edward Lovelace and James Hall, was officially selected for the festival's lineup in December 2025. It went ahead with its premiere in late January 2026, despite Courtney Love's absence and her reported desire to recut the film. The festival proceeded with the screening of the submitted version, cementing the premiere's occurrence.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **December 10, 2025**: Sundance Film Festival announces its 2026 lineup, which includes *Antiheroine*, a documentary about Courtney Love [art_culture_20260221_005_07b98da6].\n- **January 2026**: Anticipation builds for the premiere of the documentary, which covers her life in London and her sobriety.\n- **Late January 2026**: *Antiheroine* premieres at the Sundance Film Festival [art_culture_20260221_008_28d25c30].\n- **Late January 2026**: Reports emerge that Courtney Love missed the premiere and wants to recut the documentary [art_culture_20260221_009_5a807cac].\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe premiere of *Antiheroine* at Sundance was driven by its selection by the festival programmers. In December 2025, Sundance announced its lineup, which included the documentary [art_culture_20260221_005_07b98da6]. This official selection locked the film into the festival's schedule. As the festival dates approached, the filmmakers and festival organizers prepared for the screening. Despite Courtney Love reportedly wanting to recut the documentary [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8], the festival proceeded with the premiere of the submitted version, leading to its official premiere at the festival [art_culture_20260221_008_28d25c30]. \n\n## Countervailing Factors\nThe primary countervailing factor was Courtney Love's reported dissatisfaction with the cut of the film shown at Sundance. She missed the premiere and expressed a desire to recut the documentary [art_culture_20260221_009_5a807cac]. This could have led to a withdrawal of the film from the festival, but the premiere went ahead anyway, likely because the film was already scheduled and the directors/producers controlled the cut submitted to Sundance.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Sundance Film Festival announces *Antiheroine* in its 2026 lineup.\n  - Date: December 2025\n  - Why it matters causally: Confirmed the film's acceptance into the festival.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_culture_20260221_005_07b98da6]\n- E2: *Antiheroine* premieres at the Sundance Film Festival.\n  - Date: Late January 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: The direct fulfillment of the positive resolution.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_culture_20260221_008_28d25c30], [art_culture_20260221_009_5a807cac]\n- E3: Courtney Love misses the premiere and plans to recut the film.\n  - Date: Late January 2026\n  - Why it matters causally: Highlights a countervailing force (her dissatisfaction) that did not prevent the premiere.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_culture_20260221_008_28d25c30], [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sundance announces *Antiheroine* in its lineup | [art_culture_20260221_005_07b98da6] | Dec 2025 | 1.0 | Official selection. |\n| *Antiheroine* premieres at Sundance | [art_culture_20260221_008_28d25c30] | Jan 2026 | 1.0 | The premiere occurred. |\n| Courtney Love misses premiere and wants to recut | [art_culture_20260221_009_5a807cac], [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8] | Jan/Feb 2026 | 1.0 | She did not attend the screening. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe main alternative path would have been the film being pulled from the festival due to Courtney Love's objections. However, this did not happen, and the premiere proceeded as planned.\n",
