    "id": "q_culture_20260215_004_55cf4a7b",
    "title": "Will 'Antiheroine' receive a Rotten Tomatoes score of 80% or higher from critics following its Sundance premiere?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "The documentary is about a polarizing figure, which could lead to a wide range of critical reviews.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The 'Tomatometer' score on Rotten Tomatoes will be checked on this date. It must be 80% or higher based on at least 10 critic reviews.",
    "outcome": "True",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe documentary 'Antiheroine', detailing the life of Courtney Love, premiered at the 2026 Sundance Film Festival and resonated strongly with critics. The film's raw, intimate, and unfiltered portrayal of Love's past and present won widespread critical acclaim. Positive reviews highlighting its authenticity quickly pushed the movie's Rotten Tomatoes score well over the 80% threshold.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- Late January 2026: 'Antiheroine' premieres at the Sundance Film Festival, offering a deeply personal look at Courtney Love [art_culture_20250101_004_47bdeaf8].\n- February 5, 2026: Critical reviews pour in, praising the documentary's raw honesty and confirming a high critical consensus on Rotten Tomatoes [art_culture_20260205_005_0032f807].\n- February 10, 2026: Rotten Tomatoes officially lists the film with an overwhelmingly positive score, fulfilling the resolution criteria [art_culture_20260210_003_036a1a9b].\n- Mid-February 2026: Reports emerge that Love is further recutting the documentary to add more unfiltered footage, though the initial Sundance cut was already a hit [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8].\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe decision to present an uncompromising, non-linear deep dive into Courtney Love's turbulent life led directly to strong critical engagement. Critics praised the vulnerability and unfiltered access provided by director Edward Lovelace [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8]. This critical acclaim caused a rapid accumulation of positive reviews on Rotten Tomatoes. The high volume of \"Fresh\" reviews resulted in the film's score comfortably surpassing the 80% target, satisfying the positive resolution criteria.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nThe film's subject matter—involving addiction (\"If you want to nuke your life, do crack\") and past controversies—could have alienated more conservative critics or those tired of traditional rock documentaries. Furthermore, the fact that the Sundance cut was an \"unfinished\" first edit might have led to technical criticisms. However, the sheer authenticity of the material overwhelmed these potential negatives.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: 'Antiheroine' Sundance Premiere\n  - title: Sundance Premiere\n  - date: Late January 2026\n  - why it matters causally: Set the stage for critical reception.\n  - source article IDs: [art_culture_20250101_004_47bdeaf8]\n- E2: Initial Wave of Positive Critical Reviews\n  - title: Initial Wave of Positive Critical Reviews\n  - date: Early February 2026\n  - why it matters causally: Drove the Rotten Tomatoes score upward.\n  - source article IDs: [art_culture_20260205_005_0032f807]\n- E3: Rotten Tomatoes Score Tops 80%\n  - title: Rotten Tomatoes Score Tops 80%\n  - date: By February 10, 2026\n  - why it matters causally: Direct trigger for the positive resolution.\n  - source article IDs: [art_culture_20260210_003_036a1a9b]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sundance premiere and raw portrayal | [art_culture_20250101_004_47bdeaf8] | Late Jan 2026 | 0.95 | Mentions raw intimacy |\n| Positive reviews post-premiere | [art_culture_20260205_005_0032f807] | Feb 5, 2026 | 0.95 | Review scores |\n| RT score exceeds 80% | [art_culture_20260210_003_036a1a9b] | Feb 10, 2026 | 0.95 | RT page confirmation |\n| Film is recut | [art_culture_20260212_004_6e5fcfa8] | Feb 12, 2026 | 0.90 | Recutting shows perfectionism |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nIt was uncertain whether critics would embrace or reject the raw nature of Love's history. An alternative path could have seen the \"unfinished\" nature of the cut dragging down the score below 80%.\n\n",
