    "id": "q_culture_20260220_001_ef43e999",
    "title": "Will the DOJ's monopoly trial against Live Nation be delayed past its original March 2026 start date?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "Live Nation has filed a motion to delay its monopoly trial. A federal judge has already denied a motion to dismiss, clearing the case for trial.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The trial will be considered delayed if the opening arguments do not begin by March 31, 2026. This is determined by official court records.",
    "outcome": "False",
    "explanation": "## Executive Summary\nThe DOJ's monopoly trial against Live Nation was not delayed past its original March 2026 start date because it actually proceeded and concluded even earlier. A federal jury reached a verdict in mid-February 2026, finding Live Nation liable for antitrust violations. Consequently, the trial was clearly not delayed past March 2026.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **2025**: The DOJ and state attorneys general pursue an antitrust lawsuit against Live Nation and Ticketmaster.\n- **February 15, 2026**: A jury finds Live Nation illegally monopolized the ticketing market [art_business_20260215_002_a6b5e340].\n- **February 18, 2026**: Reports continue to confirm the jury's verdict against Live Nation [art_general_20260218_018_247ca4ef].\n- **February 20, 2026**: Question resolves as False since the trial was not delayed past March 2026.\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe DOJ and state AGs filed an antitrust lawsuit against Live Nation. The court scheduled the trial and pushed it forward efficiently. This led to the trial actually occurring and concluding by February 2026 [art_general_20260218_018_247ca4ef], which directly resulted in the outcome being False because it wasn't delayed past March 2026.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nLive Nation attempted to delay the proceedings by arguing that an appeals court needed to review legal questions, but the federal judge rejected these delay tactics.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Jury finds Live Nation liable in antitrust trial\n  - date: 2026-02-15\n  - title: Jury finds Live Nation liable in antitrust trial\n  - why it matters causally: Proves the trial happened.\n  - source article IDs: [art_business_20260215_002_a6b5e340]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Jury finds Live Nation liable | [art_business_20260215_002_a6b5e340] | 2026-02-15 | 1.0 | Confirms the trial concluded. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nNone, the trial already concluded.\n",
    "is_polymarket": false,
    "is_overlap": false,
