    "id": "q_culture_20260222_008_b89139bd",
    "title": "Will John Davidson be banned from attending future BAFTA ceremonies?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "The shouting of a racial slur by John Davidson at the BAFTA awards has led to a public outcry, putting pressure on the organization to take action.",
    "resolution_criteria": "This question will resolve to YES if BAFTA announces that John Davidson is no longer welcome at their events. This is a forecast on BAFTA's response to the incident.",
    "outcome": "False",
    "explanation": "## Executive Summary\nJohn Davidson was not banned from attending future BAFTA ceremonies. Following his controversial removal from the BAFTA Games Awards for inappropriate behavior, BAFTA conducted a formal review. They concluded that while his actions were unacceptable, they did not merit a permanent ban, resulting in a formal warning instead. Thus, the ground truth outcome is False.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- 2026-02-21: John Davidson makes controversial remarks/actions leading to his removal from the BAFTA Games Awards venue.\n- 2026-02-21: Following the incident, widespread speculation begins regarding his future at BAFTA ceremonies.\n- 2026-02-22: BAFTA issues a formal statement confirming that he will not be banned from attending future ceremonies, but instead issues a formal warning.\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\n- Davidson's behavior led to an immediate response and temporary removal from the venue because it violated the event's code of conduct.\n- This triggered the BAFTA disciplinary committee to convene and review the event.\n- The committee determined that a formal warning was sufficient, which resulted in the final outcome that he will not be banned from attending future ceremonies.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\n- Public outcry and media pressure initially pushed for a strict ban or revocation of his awards.\n- Some members of the community argued for his permanent exclusion. These were overwhelmed by the committee's decision that his actions did not cross the threshold for a lifetime ban.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- Event 1: Davidson's initial actions and removal.\n  - Date: 2026-02-21\n  - Why it matters: Triggered the backlash and formal review.\n  - Article IDs: [art_culture_20260223_002_bb29d3a9, art_general_20260223_011_607c603a]\n- Event 2: BAFTA issues formal warning instead of ban.\n  - Date: 2026-02-22\n  - Why it matters: The direct cause of the negative resolution.\n  - Article IDs: [art_general_20260223_010_46fffd6d, art_general_20260223_017_0f309bb3]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Davidson removed | [art_general_20260223_011_607c603a] | 2026-02-21 | 0.9 | Temporary measure |\n| BAFTA warning | [art_general_20260223_010_46fffd6d] | 2026-02-22 | 1.0 | Final decision |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\n- If the media pressure had been stronger or if previous severe infractions existed, BAFTA might have opted for a permanent ban.\n",
