    "title": "Will the pandemic comedy, if released, receive a 'Rotten' score (below 60%) on Rotten Tomatoes from critics?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "Satirical films, especially those with a political angle, often receive mixed or poor reviews from professional critics.",
    "resolution_criteria": "This is a predictive question. The Tomatometer score will be checked one month after the film's initial release, if it occurs.",
    "outcome": "True",
    "explanation": "\n# Required Output Format (use these exact section headings)\n\n## Executive Summary\nThe pandemic comedy failed to resonate with critics, ultimately receiving a 'Rotten' score on Rotten Tomatoes. The humor was seen as dated and insensitive, leading to widespread negative reviews. The final score settled well below the 60% threshold for a 'Fresh' rating.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- Early production: The movie was announced as a satire of pandemic life. [art_culture_20220401_002_d5d57544]\n- 2022-04-01: Critics released their initial reviews, panning the film. [art_culture_20220401_003_de80dc64]\n- Pre-2026-02-22: The movie's Rotten Tomatoes score stabilized below 60%. [art_culture_20220401_004_45e84bd4]\n- 2026-02-22: The question resolves as True since the score remained 'Rotten'. [art_culture_20220401_005_7ca72c99]\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe movie's dated humor and awkward handling of sensitive pandemic topics caused an immediate backlash from critics. This backlash led to a surge of negative reviews upon release. Because the negative reviews vastly outnumbered the positive ones, it resulted in a 'Rotten' score on Rotten Tomatoes. The critical consensus remained negative over time, which ultimately triggered the True resolution of the question. [art_culture_20220401_002_d5d57544]\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nSome audiences appreciated the slapstick humor, but this failed to overwhelm the critics' consensus, who focus more on thematic coherence and timing.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1\n    - title: Movie release and review embargo lift\n    - date: 2022-04-01\n    - why it matters causally: Allowed critics to publish their negative reviews, establishing the initial Rotten score.\n    - source article IDs: art_culture_20220401_002_d5d57544\n- E2\n    - title: Question resolution date reached\n    - date: 2026-02-22\n    - why it matters causally: Fixed the timeframe for the final score check.\n    - source article IDs: art_culture_20220401_004_45e84bd4\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Negative critical reception | art_culture_20220401_002_d5d57544 | 2022-04-01 | 0.9 | Strong consensus |\n| Rotten Tomatoes score below 60% | art_culture_20220401_003_de80dc64 | 2022-04-01 | 0.9 | Score stabilized |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nIf the humor had been more universally accepted, it might have skirted the 60% line.\n",
