    "id": "q_culture_20260222_037_c6e2dd51",
    "title": "Was Peter Attia fired by CBS News or did he resign?",
    "question_type": "mcq",
    "options": [
      "Fired",
      "Resigned"
    ],
    "background": "Following the disclosure of his correspondence with Jeffrey Epstein, Peter Attia is no longer a contributor at CBS News. The nature of his departure is a key detail.",
    "resolution_criteria": "This will be determined by the reporting of reputable news outlets like The Hollywood Reporter, which broke the story.",
    "outcome": "Resigned",
    "explanation": "\n# Executive Summary\nDr. Peter Attia, a celebrity wellness doctor and medical influencer, resigned from his recently announced contributor role at CBS News in February 2026. This departure was triggered by the release of Justice Department documents showing he had exchanged personal and lewd emails with convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein in 2016. Amidst intense public backlash from his fanbase and the broader public over these communications, Attia chose to step down to avoid becoming a distraction to the network, despite some internal inclinations at CBS to keep him on.\n\n# Timeline Of Key Events\n- January 2026: Peter Attia is named as one of 19 new contributors to CBS News, part of a new strategy by Bari Weiss to revamp the network's offerings.\n- Early February 2026: The U.S. Justice Department releases a trove of Epstein files, which include 2016 emails between Attia and Jeffrey Epstein containing lewd remarks. [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n- Early February 2026: Following the release of the documents, Attia issues a statement apologizing and clarifying that he was not involved in any criminal activity and had never visited Epstein's properties. [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n- February 23, 2026: A spokesperson announces that Attia has resigned from his CBS News contributor position, stating that he \"stepped back to ensure his involvement didn’t become a distraction.\" [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n\n# Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of Peter Attia's departure was his past association and correspondence with Jeffrey Epstein in 2016. The intermediate mechanism was the public release of these communications in early February 2026 by the U.S. Justice Department, which revealed lewd exchanges. This release triggered a strong negative reaction and backlash from the public and his fans. The proximate trigger for his exit was the mounting pressure from this backlash, which led to his decision to resign from CBS News to prevent his controversy from distracting the network, as stated by his spokesperson [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b].\n\n# Countervailing Factors\nThe main countervailing factor was the reported inclination of Bari Weiss, the head of CBS News who brought Attia on, to allow him to remain as a network contributor despite the controversy [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]. However, this internal support was overwhelmed by the magnitude of the public backlash and Attia's own assessment that his continued presence would be detrimental to the network's reputation.\n\n# Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Peter Attia named as a CBS News contributor.\n  - Date: January 2026\n  - Causal significance: Established his employment relationship with the network.\n  - Article IDs: [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n- E2: Release of Epstein files containing Attia's emails.\n  - Date: Early February 2026\n  - Causal significance: Sparked the controversy that ultimately led to his resignation.\n  - Article IDs: [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n- E3: Public backlash against Peter Attia.\n  - Date: February 2026\n  - Causal significance: Created the pressure and untenable situation that prompted his departure.\n  - Article IDs: [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n- E4: Peter Attia resigns from CBS News.\n  - Date: February 23, 2026\n  - Causal significance: The final outcome of the sequence of events.\n  - Article IDs: [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b]\n\n# Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Attia named CBS contributor | [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b] | Jan 2026 | 1.0 | Part of Bari Weiss strategy |\n| Epstein files released showing emails | [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b] | Early Feb 2026 | 1.0 | Included lewd messages from 2016 |\n| Attia resigns from CBS News | [art_general_20260223_019_dcfe321b] | Feb 23, 2026 | 1.0 | Resigned to avoid being a distraction |\n\n# Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThere is minimal uncertainty about the sequence of events and the final outcome. An alternative path could have been CBS News outright firing him, but reports consistently state he resigned or \"stepped back\" of his own accord, likely to preempt further damage to his or the network's brand.\n",
