    "id": "q_finance_20260222_008_58ef6fbb",
    "title": "When will Eli Lilly's acquisition of Orna Therapeutics be completed?",
    "question_type": "timeframe",
    "options": [
      "2026-02-20"
    ],
    "background": "Eli Lilly announced its intention to acquire Orna Therapeutics for $2.4 billion on February 9, 2026.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The official date of completion of the acquisition, as announced by either Eli Lilly or Orna Therapeutics.",
    "outcome": "2026-02-20",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nOn February 9, 2026, Eli Lilly announced a definitive agreement to acquire Orna Therapeutics for up to $2.4 billion. Orna Therapeutics specializes in engineered circular RNA (oRNA) technology paired with lipid nanoparticle (LNP) delivery to create in vivo CAR-T therapies. The transaction required standard regulatory reviews, including the expiration of the HSR waiting period. Following the satisfaction of these customary closing conditions without major regulatory challenge, the acquisition was officially completed on February 20, 2026.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **February 9, 2026**: Eli Lilly announces the definitive agreement to acquire Orna Therapeutics for up to $2.4 billion in upfront cash and milestones. ([art_health_20260209_002_a490c181], [art_health_20260209_004_47eab2b9], [art_health_20260209_006_bef278b4])\n- **February 9, 2026 - February 19, 2026**: The acquisition undergoes standard regulatory review under the Hart-Scott-Rodino (HSR) Act, checking for antitrust concerns. The waiting period expires without significant pushback.\n- **February 20, 2026**: Eli Lilly officially completes the acquisition of Orna Therapeutics. ([art_business_20260220_003_a70024b1])\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\n- **Strategic interest in in vivo CAR-T therapy**: Eli Lilly aimed to diversify its portfolio, specifically focusing on expanding its immunology pipeline and leveraging \"off-the-shelf\" in vivo CAR-T therapy for autoimmune diseases. This led to their interest in Orna Therapeutics. ([art_health_20260209_006_bef278b4])\n- **Acquisition Agreement**: This strategic interest resulted in the definitive agreement announced on February 9, 2026, where Eli Lilly agreed to acquire Orna Therapeutics for up to $2.4 billion. ([art_health_20260209_002_a490c181])\n- **Regulatory Clearance**: The relatively small upfront size of the deal (implied, given total milestone value is $2.4B) and the novel, non-overlapping nature of Orna's early-stage in vivo platform triggered no major antitrust challenges, leading to the expiration of the HSR waiting period.\n- **Completion**: With all regulatory and customary closing conditions met, the acquisition officially closed on February 20, 2026. ([art_business_20260220_003_a70024b1])\n\n## Countervailing Factors\n- **FTC Antitrust Scrutiny**: Recent years have seen increased FTC scrutiny of pharmaceutical acquisitions. However, since Orna is a clinical-stage startup with novel technology (in vivo CAR-T) and no currently marketed overlapping products with Lilly, the acquisition did not present standard monopolistic threats, meaning regulatory pushback failed to materialize.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: Eli Lilly announces agreement to acquire Orna Therapeutics\n  - date: 2026-02-09\n  - why it matters causally: Initiated the formal acquisition process and established the terms of the deal.\n  - source article IDs: [art_health_20260209_002_a490c181], [art_health_20260209_006_bef278b4]\n- E2: HSR Waiting Period expires / Regulatory clearance obtained\n  - date: 2026-02-10 to 2026-02-19\n  - why it matters causally: A necessary legal condition for the deal to close, preventing antitrust blocks.\n  - source article IDs: [art_business_20260220_003_a70024b1]\n- E3: Eli Lilly completes Orna Therapeutics acquisition\n  - date: 2026-02-20\n  - why it matters causally: The final realization of the outcome.\n  - source article IDs: [art_business_20260220_003_a70024b1]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Eli Lilly announces acquisition of Orna Therapeutics for up to $2.4B | [art_health_20260209_002_a490c181], [art_health_20260209_006_bef278b4] | 2026-02-09 | 1.0 | Official announcement details. |\n| Completion of the acquisition | [art_business_20260220_003_a70024b1] | 2026-02-20 | 1.0 | Final close confirmation. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\n- The exact upfront cash amount versus milestone payments was not heavily detailed in initial public announcements.\n- A possible alternative path would have been extended FTC review causing a delay in completion if they deemed the platform a threat to future market competition.\n",
