    "id": "q_health_20260220_029_0d65eed5",
    "title": "When will a verdict or settlement be reached in the OhioHealth antitrust lawsuit?",
    "question_type": "timeframe",
    "options": [
      "2025-11-15T00:00:00Z"
    ],
    "background": "The lawsuit against OhioHealth is expected to be a lengthy legal battle.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The date of the verdict or settlement will be a matter of public record.",
    "outcome": "2025-11-15T00:00:00Z",
    "explanation": "\n# Executive Summary\nThe OhioHealth antitrust lawsuit concluded with a settlement reached on November 15, 2025. This outcome was primarily driven by overwhelming legal pressure from both federal and state authorities, leading OhioHealth to agree to modify its contracting practices rather than face a protracted legal battle.\n\n# Timeline Of Key Events\n- **February 2025**: The Department of Justice and Ohio Attorney General initiated investigations into OhioHealth's alleged anticompetitive practices. [art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218]\n- **Mid-2025**: Increased pressure and preliminary findings indicated strong evidence of contractual restrictions preventing budget-conscious health plans.\n- **November 15, 2025**: A comprehensive settlement was finalized between OhioHealth, the DOJ, and the state of Ohio, avoiding a full trial.\n\n# Causal Chain Analysis\nThe investigation by the DOJ and Ohio AG uncovered anticompetitive contract terms that blocked payers from offering tiered or narrow network plans [art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218]. This regulatory scrutiny **caused** significant reputational and financial risks for OhioHealth. The mounting evidence **led to** accelerated settlement negotiations. Ultimately, the desire to avoid prolonged litigation and potential punitive damages **resulted in** the settlement on November 15, 2025.\n\n# Countervailing Factors\nInitially, OhioHealth maintained confidence in its legal position, cooperating but steadfast in defending its managed care agreements. However, the combined force of federal and state resources overwhelmed their defensive posture.\n\n# Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1: DOJ and Ohio AG launch investigation into OhioHealth (Feb 2025) [art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218]\n- E2: Settlement reached (Nov 15, 2025) [art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218]\n\n# Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| DOJ Investigation | art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218 | 2025 | 0.9 | Allegations of anticompetitive practices |\n| Settlement Reached | art_general_20260220_007_8d15b218 | Nov 15, 2025 | 0.9 | Final resolution |\n\n# Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nIt was initially uncertain if OhioHealth would litigate the matter to a verdict. An alternative path would have seen a lengthy trial extending well into 2026 or 2027.\n",
    "is_polymarket": false,
    "is_overlap": false,
    "market_open": "2025-02-20T00:00:00+00:00",
    "market_open_estimated": false,
