    "id": "q_sports_20251031_072_75ddc785",
    "title": "Who will win the 2025 World Series?",
    "question_type": "mcq",
    "options": [
      "Los Angeles Dodgers",
      "New York Yankees",
      "Other"
    ],
    "background": "The World Series is the championship series of Major League Baseball (MLB).",
    "resolution_criteria": "The winner will be the team that wins the 2025 World Series.",
    "outcome": "Los Angeles Dodgers",
    "explanation": "\n## Executive Summary\nThe Los Angeles Dodgers won the 2025 World Series by fielding an exceptionally talented and historically expensive roster. The Dodgers set an MLB spending record with a final payroll reaching over $500 million, seven times the lowest-spending team, assembling a star-studded lineup that dominated throughout the season. Their massive investments culminated in securing the championship and further establishing their status as one of the elite franchises of the past 25 years.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **March 4, 2025**: The Dodgers are recognized as closing in on the No. 1 team of the past 25 years, highlighting their long-term dominance and high expectations for the season ([art_general_20250304_002_8f66f3ec]).\n- **October 2025**: The Dodgers advance through the playoffs, showcasing the strength of their historic payroll.\n- **October 31, 2025**: The Dodgers win the 2025 World Series. Their spending strategy was later highlighted as smashing the MLB record for payroll on a championship roster, surpassing $515 million ([art_sports_20251031_002_5c6dbd71], [art_sports_20251031_003_e0980b95]).\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of the Dodgers' 2025 World Series victory was their unprecedented financial investment in the roster, which smashed the MLB spending record ([art_sports_20251031_002_5c6dbd71]). This led to the assembly of an unparalleled collection of talent, creating depth and star power that overwhelmed opponents throughout the season and the playoffs. This intermediate mechanism of maintaining a healthy, elite core ultimately triggered their success in the postseason, resulting in the 2025 World Series title.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nThe New York Yankees and other contenders posed significant threats. The Yankees attempted to bounce back from injuries and defensive issues, with players like Trent Grisham vowing to improve ([art_sports_20251031_010_7e62f3a9]), and the return of their ace Gerrit Cole ([art_sports_20251031_007_dd00e0da]). However, these factors failed to overcome the Dodgers' immense financial advantages and sheer roster depth.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- **E1**: Dodgers set MLB payroll record.\n  - title: Dodgers set MLB payroll record\n  - date: 2025 Season\n  - why it matters causally: Allowed them to assemble a historically deep and talented roster.\n  - source article IDs: [art_sports_20251031_002_5c6dbd71], [art_sports_20251031_003_e0980b95]\n- **E2**: Dodgers win 2025 World Series.\n  - title: Dodgers win 2025 World Series\n  - date: October 2025\n  - why it matters causally: The direct final outcome of the question.\n  - source article IDs: [art_sports_20251031_002_5c6dbd71]\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Dodgers break payroll record | [art_sports_20251031_002_5c6dbd71], [art_sports_20251031_003_e0980b95] | 2025 Season | 1.0 | Spent over $515 million |\n| Dodgers ranked as top franchise | [art_general_20250304_002_8f66f3ec] | March 2025 | 0.9 | High expectations |\n| Yankees face injuries and defensive struggles | [art_sports_20251031_010_7e62f3a9], [art_sports_20251031_007_dd00e0da] | 2025 Season | 0.9 | Countervailing factors |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe main uncertainty during the season revolved around whether the Dodgers' massive spending would translate into a championship or if the pressure would lead to an early playoff exit. An alternative path involved the Yankees or Phillies overcoming their respective hurdles to secure the title, but their rosters lacked the historic depth of the Dodgers.\n",
    "is_polymarket": false,
    "is_overlap": false,
    "market_open": "2025-03-01T00:00:00+00:00",
    "market_open_estimated": false,
    "market_close": "2025-10-31T23:59:59+00:00",
