    "id": "q_sports_20260108_014_46907273",
    "title": "Will the WWE faction 'The Vision' officially disband by the end of 2026?",
    "question_type": "binary",
    "options": [
      "Yes",
      "No"
    ],
    "background": "No background available.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The faction will be considered disbanded if WWE officially announces it or if the members begin feuding with each other.",
    "outcome": "True",
    "explanation": "\n# Required Output Format\n\n## Executive Summary\nThe WWE faction 'The Vision' officially disbanded by the end of 2025, confirming the positive resolution of the question. The primary cause of the disbandment was an untimely injury to the faction's leader, Seth Rollins, which forced WWE creative to scrap their long-term storyline plans. Originally intended to feud with Roman Reigns and disband after WrestleMania 42, the faction lost its momentum without Rollins. Consequently, WWE made the decision to quietly dissolve the group in mid-December 2025, and former members began pursuing new storylines.\n\n## Timeline Of Key Events\n- **October/November 2025**: Seth Rollins suffers an injury during a match with Cody Rhodes, derailing long-term creative plans for 'The Vision' [art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8].\n- **December 3, 2025**: Reports reveal the original plan was for Bron Breakker to usurp Seth Rollins and take over 'The Vision' post-WrestleMania 42 [art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8].\n- **December 15, 2025**: WWE officially but quietly disbands 'The Vision' following the pivot in creative direction due to Rollins' injury [art_sports_20251215_016_b351a37f].\n- **January 5, 2026**: Former 'Vision' members are seen hinting at new alliances on social media, cementing the faction's end [art_sports_20260105_021_710b47f9].\n\n## Causal Chain Analysis\nThe dissolution of 'The Vision' was primarily **caused** by the real-life injury sustained by Seth Rollins [art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8]. This injury **led to** WWE creative having to dramatically pivot from their established long-term plans, which originally involved 'The Vision' persisting until after WrestleMania 42. Without their key central figure, the faction lacked narrative direction, which **resulted in** WWE officials deciding to cut their losses. This **triggered** the quiet disbandment of the group in December 2025 [art_sports_20251215_016_b351a37f], well before the 2026 deadline.\n\n## Countervailing Factors\nThe main countervailing factor was WWE's initial long-term booking strategy. WWE prefers to map out storylines months in advance, and 'The Vision' was slated to remain a cohesive unit until at least WrestleMania 42 [art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8]. Had Rollins not been injured, the faction would likely have survived into early 2026. However, the severity of the injury and the need to shuffle top-card storylines around Roman Reigns and Cody Rhodes overwhelmed the original plan.\n\n## Event Candidate Inventory\n- E1\n    - title: Seth Rollins sustains injury\n    - date: Late 2025\n    - why it matters causally: Forced a rewrite of WWE creative plans, removing the faction's focal point.\n    - source article IDs: art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8\n- E2\n    - title: 'The Vision' officially disbanded\n    - date: 2025-12-15\n    - why it matters causally: The direct resolution of the question, establishing that the faction no longer exists.\n    - source article IDs: art_sports_20251215_016_b351a37f\n\n## Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Seth Rollins injured, changing plans | art_sports_20251203_003_6e6548b8 | 2025-12-03 | 1.0 | Detailed report on changed WrestleMania plans. |\n| 'The Vision' disbanded | art_sports_20251215_016_b351a37f | 2025-12-15 | 1.0 | Explicit confirmation of disbandment. |\n| Members hint at new alliances | art_sports_20260105_021_710b47f9 | 2026-01-05 | 0.9 | Confirms members moved on. |\n\n## Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\nThe primary uncertainty was whether WWE might have kept the faction alive under Bron Breakker's leadership immediately after Rollins' injury, as initially planned for post-WrestleMania. An alternative path could have seen Breakker take over early, keeping the faction intact through 2026, but WWE opted to disband them entirely instead.\n",
