    "id": "q_sports_20260221_002_678d1b1d",
    "title": "Who will win the 2026 Autotrader 400 NASCAR race?",
    "question_type": "mcq",
    "options": [
      "Carson Hocevar",
      "Kyle Larson",
      "Denny Hamlin",
      "Other"
    ],
    "background": "Articles 13, 14, and 15 discuss the upcoming NASCAR race, highlighting Carson Hocevar as a favored driver.",
    "resolution_criteria": "The question resolves to the name of the driver who is declared the official winner of the 2026 Autotrader 400 race at Atlanta Motor Speedway.",
    "outcome": "Carson Hocevar",
    "explanation": "\n# Executive Summary\nThe 2026 Autotrader 400 NASCAR race at EchoPark Speedway resulted in a major victory for Carson Hocevar. During the practice and qualifying rounds, Hocevar demonstrated strong pacing, but it was key pit stop adjustments and late-race caution flags that determined the outcome. In the final stage, an incident involving front-runners forced a restart where Hocevar aggressively overtook the leaders. Aided by superior tire management and a well-timed block on Denny Hamlin, Hocevar secured the win.\n\n# Timeline Of Key Events\n- **2026-02-19**: Practice and qualifying sessions indicated strong pacing from Carson Hocevar and Denny Hamlin [art_sports_20260219_012_3f10e505].\n- **2026-02-22**: Early Race - The 2026 Autotrader 400 commenced with early dominators leading the initial laps [art_general_20260222_002_550f1cc3].\n- **2026-02-22**: Stage 2 - Tire degradation affected several teams, prompting crucial pit strategies. Carson Hocevar's team opted for aggressive adjustments [art_sports_20260222_004_244dff7e].\n- **2026-02-22**: Final Stage - A multi-car incident triggered a caution, resetting the field and placing Hocevar in contention [art_sports_20260222_006_c4de671c].\n- **2026-02-22**: Final Laps - Hocevar executed a decisive pass on the restart and held off the pack to claim victory [art_sports_20260222_007_3eca2b1a].\n\n# Causal Chain Analysis\nThe root cause of the outcome was Hocevar's underlying car setup emphasizing late-run tire longevity, which caused his car to perform optimally during the final stage [art_sports_20260219_014_6f88d6e0]. This mechanical advantage triggered an intermediate mechanism where Hocevar could maintain speed while others struggled with tire wear [art_sports_20260222_005_06435a20]. The proximate trigger for the victory was the late-race caution flag, which resulted in a bunched-up field and allowed Hocevar to use his superior handling to overtake the race leader on the restart [art_sports_20260222_008_c1b88a21]. Because of his team's flawless final pit stop and his aggressive drafting technique, this led directly to Hocevar securing the win [art_general_20260222_010_cfca116f].\n\n# Countervailing Factors\n- Denny Hamlin and Kyle Larson both possessed strong initial pacing and led multiple laps early in the race. \n- However, their strategies failed because they prioritized short-run speed, leaving their tires excessively degraded during the decisive long runs in the final stage, which overwhelmed their ability to defend against Hocevar's advances.\n\n# Event Candidate Inventory\n- **E1**: Practice and Qualifying strong performance\n  - Date: 2026-02-19\n  - Why it matters causally: Established Hocevar as a competitive force and validated the late-run setup.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260219_012_3f10e505]\n- **E2**: Mid-race strategic pit adjustments\n  - Date: 2026-02-22\n  - Why it matters causally: Fine-tuned the car's handling for the critical final stage, enabling the eventual overtake.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260222_004_244dff7e]\n- **E3**: Late-race caution and restart\n  - Date: 2026-02-22\n  - Why it matters causally: Closed the gap to the leaders, providing the immediate opportunity for Hocevar to take the lead.\n  - Source article IDs: [art_sports_20260222_006_c4de671c]\n\n# Evidence Mapping Table\n| Claim/Event | Article IDs | Date Support | Confidence (0-1) | Notes |\n|-------------|-------------|--------------|------------------|-------|\n| Practice pacing validation | [art_sports_20260219_012_3f10e505] | 2026-02-19 | 0.9 | Strong early indicators |\n| Tire management strategy | [art_sports_20260222_004_244dff7e] | 2026-02-22 | 0.85 | Critical to long-run success |\n| Late-race restart execution | [art_sports_20260222_006_c4de671c], [art_sports_20260222_008_c1b88a21] | 2026-02-22 | 0.95 | The defining moment of the race |\n\n# Uncertainties And Alternative Paths\n- If the late-race caution had not occurred, Kyle Larson might have maintained his lead to the finish.\n- Uncertainties remain regarding whether a different tire compound selection by opposing teams could have neutralized Hocevar's advantage in the final 20 laps.\n",
